A||||4||Lynx||Brake Drag||||1||
Z||000000||Lynx||12-19-1999||08:39 AM||||My 85 SC's rear brakes drag quite a bit. I rebuilt them both because one was leaking and they both drag now. The wheel still turn even with the tire off but it takes a little effort. Now i dont know what to do just buy new ones or is there a way to fix them? I cant hardly even try to pull them back of the rotor. Also i pulled the whole suspension of the driver side rear wheel (change clutch) Now i put it back together and the car pulls to the right. Can the alignment on that rear wheel make a Big difference?<P>Thanks for any reply's <BR>Lynx||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||12-19-1999||10:59 AM||||I'd check the e-brake cables first, sounds like they may not be releasing all the way. Anytime you have the rear struts off or replace the rear struts, you need to have the car realigned.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||12-19-1999||03:13 PM||||I think Lynx means he pulled the driver side rear suspension as an assembly. All you do is: take off p.brake cable, disconnect brake hoses, break tie-rod from spindle, remove pinch bolt from ball joint, and remove the three strut bolts from up top. When re-installed alignment is the same as when removed. Ed Parks recommends doing it this way to preserve alignment when doing a clutch replacement.<P>I may have read Lynx' post wrong though.<BR>When does the car pull? Only accelleration, deceleration, braking, all the time?<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 12-19-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Lynx||12-21-1999||12:44 PM||||Unfortunetly i pulled the whole strut not knowing what i was doing and it pulls to the right all the time. I have a bad inner tie rod on the pass side. I noticed the wheel hung to the right just a little so i tightned the tierod and pulled the wheel strait and it dosent pull half as bad now but it does still drift but not pull to the right. So im not worried about that now. Im worried about the brake drag. The ebrake is releasing completly. I beliave the front calipers might be dragging too, they get hotter than the back. Ill check if they are tommorow. Is the somthing else that could make them all drag?<P>Lynx||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||12-21-1999||05:38 PM||||It is normal for the front brakes to get hotter than the rear. The reason being the front brakes do the majority of stopping the car. Only 20-30% of the work is done by the rear brakes.||||reg||1
